===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|trompe l'œil|trompe l’œil}}, {{l|en|trompe-l'oeil|trompe-l’oeil}}, {{l|en|trompe-l'œil|trompe-l’œil}}

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|trompe-l'œil|trompe-l’œil|trompe l’oeil|lit=deceives the eye|lang=la}}, from {{term|trompe|lang=fr}} (“deceives”, the third-person singular indicative simple present form of {{term|tromper|lang=fr}}, “to deceive”) + {{term|l'|l’|lang=fr}} (“[[t'|t’]]”, the prevocalic form of {{term|le|lang=fr}}, “the”) + {{term|œil||eye|lang=fr}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{enPR|tʀôɴp löy}}, {{IPA|/tʁɔ̃p lœj/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/tR\O_~p l9j/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[tromper#French|trompe]] [[le#French|l’]][[œil#French|oeil]]|-|pl='''trompe l’oeil''' ''or'' '''[[trompe l'oeil#English|trompe l’oeils]]'''; see [[#Usage notes|the usage note]]}}

# {{uncountable}} A [[genre]] of [[still life]] [[painting]] that exploits human [[vision]] to create the [[illusion]] that the [[subject]] of the painting is real.
# {{countable}} A painting of this kind.

====Usage notes====
* This phrase is sometimes misconstructed as {{term|trompe d'œil|trompe d’œil|lang=en}} and {{term|trompe-d'œil|trompe-d’œil|lang=en}}, which, literally interpreted in French, means “deceives ''of'' eye”.
* In French, {{term|trompe-l'œil|trompe-l’œil|lang=fr}} is an [[invariant]] noun; the same usage is reflected in the plural use of the English {{term||trompe l’oeil|lang=en}}. Alternatively, {{term||trompe l’oeil|lang=en}} is treated as a [[headless]] noun phrase, to which is suffixed {{term|-s|lang=en}} to form a regular plural form. Still otherwise, some authors form novel plurals on modified etymological bases, such as the technically correct {{term|trompent-l'œil|trompent-l’œil|[they] deceive the eye|lang=en}} and the ultimately mistaken {{term|trompe les yeux|trompe les yeux|deceives the eyes|lang=en}}; however, such neologistic constructions are vanishingly rare.

